      "textEn": "344\n\nBecause atheists and evil people do not go to the refuge of God. Therefore, Lord Krishna, being complete himself, even after being bound, wants from the bound souls in various eras that they surrender to him, so that they can be freed from the worldly\nbondage. The summary is that the more we engage in devotion to Krishna and serve God,\nthe more we benefit. Krishna does not need any kind of service from us.\nHe does not want it. Therefore, I, being free from all anxieties,\ngrasp the Lord with all my being, as wise men do. He who has entered the abode of the qualities of the lower-born.\nHe who is purified by the one who is not described by the lower-born. 12>. Meaning of the word\n\nTherefore,\nI, leaving aside the thought of being unworthy,\nhaving taken refuge in God,\nwill sing or describe, according to my intellect,\nthat which is according to my intellect,\nthough born in a lower caste (my father was an Asura and devoid of all virtues),\nbecause of ignorance,\nthe abandonment of qualities,\nmaterial\nOf the world (which is born according to the impurity of the qualities of being)—entered into—within—entered—into—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—polluted—by—poll Therefore, even though I have taken birth in the demon clan, undoubtedly, as far as my intellect goes,\nI will pray to God with all my effort. Whichever person, due to ignorance, is compelled to enter this material\nworld, he can make material life pure if he\nprays to God and listens to His praise. Meaning: It is clear that a devotee does not need to be born in a high family, be rich, have a royal nature, or be beautiful. None of these virtues can be attached to any one devotion. He should have such an experience in devotion, \"God is great and I am very small.\" Therefore, it is my duty that\nI pray to God.\"On this basis, God can be understood and his service\ncan be done.\nIn the Bhagavad Gita (18.55), the Lord says—\n\nBy devotion, one knows Me; by what else do I exist? Then, knowing the mother, they contemplate the essence, and afterwards."
